<scaenae>
  <prospectus titulus="hut-hearth" pictura="casa_focus">
    <descriptio>
      A low room of logs, warm after the clearing. A fire burns in a
      stone hearth and throws its light across the floor; a pot hangs
      over it. Daylight comes in at one window. Someone lives here,
      and has not gone far: the candle on the table is still lit.
    </descriptio>
    <res titulus="hearth">
      The stones are black with years of smoke. Whatever is in the
      pot has been simmering a long while. It smells of onions, and
      of something you cannot name.
    </res>
    <res titulus="window">
      Through the glass: grass, the green hill, and a sky so clear
      you can count the specks in it.
    </res>
    <res titulus="jars">
      Three jars on a shelf. Honey, by the colour. Salt. The third
      is stoppered tight, and you would rather not shake it.
    </res>
    <res titulus="book">
      A ledger, ruled by hand. Every line is a date and a tally of
      firewood. The last entry is today.
    </res>
    <res titulus="turn" exitus="hut-door">
      You turn your back to the fire.
    </res>
  </prospectus>

  <prospectus titulus="hut-door" pictura="casa_ostium">
    <descriptio>
      The other end of the room. The door you came in by, a coat and
      a hat on their pegs, a narrow bed made up with a woven blanket.
      A small window in the side wall lets a square of light fall on
      the floor. The fire is at your back now.
    </descriptio>
    <res titulus="door" exitus="mundus">
      Planks, braced and pegged. The clearing is outside, where you
      left it.
    </res>
    <res titulus="coat">
      Heavy wool, mended at both elbows. The pockets are empty except
      for a length of twine and one acorn.
    </res>
    <res titulus="bed">
      Narrow and neatly made. The blanket is woven in a pattern of
      diamonds, red on cream. Nobody has slept in it today.
    </res>
    <res titulus="turn" exitus="hut-hearth">
      You turn back to the fire.
    </res>
  </prospectus>
</scaenae>
